{
  "id": "pip-resolution-impossible",
  "title": "pip ResolutionImpossible: pydantic 2 pin conflicts with internal acme-feature-store",
  "description": "A PR migrating example-org/ml-features to pydantic v2 bumps requirements.txt from pydantic==1.10.18 to pydantic==2.9.2 (and adds pydantic-settings), but the internal package acme-feature-store==3.2.0, still pinned in the same file, declares pydantic<2.0,>=1.10.13. pip stops in 'Install dependencies' with ResolutionImpossible before any test runs; test (3.12) is only cancelled by fail-fast and build-wheel is skipped. The code changes in the diff are a red herring: nothing was imported. The correct answer names pydantic and the conflict with acme-feature-store, and the fix belongs in requirements.txt (keep pydantic<2 until acme-feature-store ships a pydantic-2 compatible release, or upgrade acme-feature-store together with the bump).",
